        rules: {
          objective: 'Capture cards from the table by matching their values. Score points for capturing specific cards (Kings, the 7 of Coins, etc.) and for capturing the most cards overall.',
          gameplay: "1. Players take turns playing one card from hand to the table. 2. If the played card matches the value of a card on the table, the player captures both cards. 3. Multiple cards can be captured if their values sum to the played card's value. 4. If no capture is possible, the card remains on the table. 5. After playing, players draw a replacement card from the stock if available.",
          keyRules: [
            'Play one card per turn',
            'Capture cards of matching value',
            'Draw replacement card after playing',
            'Score for specific captured cards and sweeps',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Remember which cards have been played. Try to capture Kings and the 7 of Coins. Avoid leaving valuable cards on the table for opponents to capture.',
          intermediate: 'Set up sweeps by leaving specific card combinations on the table that you can capture on your next turn. Force opponents to play cards that benefit you.',
          advanced: "Card counting is essential. Track all high-value cards to predict opponents' holdings. Sacrifice immediate captures to set up multiple captures or sweeps.",
          tips: [
            'The 7 of Coins is usually the most valuable single card - prioritize capturing it',
            'Leaving a single low card on the table is safer than multiple cards that can be combined',
            'When you have multiple capture options, choose the one that leaves the table least favorable for opponents',
          ],
